-- check/bad: §10.10. `blank` is a `pub` value of NO beni parameters and a
-- NON-function type whose inferred scheme carries `k.compare`. A value that
-- needs a method has to receive it, which would make `blank` a thunk of one
-- hidden argument (§8.1, checker-v2.md §12.5) and change what its type says
-- across the module boundary, so the checker refuses it.
--
-- It must be UNANNOTATED: with `pub blank : Dict k v` the annotation
-- declares `k` rigid with an empty constraint set and the body's requirement
-- is `missing_where_constraint` (§10.4) instead. And its type must not be a
-- function: `pub equals = (==)` is accepted, see
-- `run/ConstrainedPubFunctionConstant/`.
import Dict


pub blank =
    Dict.fromList []
